  "release_identity": "Kotoba 1.0.0 build 32: displayed-reading speech and roadmap return position fixes",
  "changes": [
    "Every reading-aware speech button uses the entry/card's own kana rather than ambiguous raw kanji. Roadmap, vocabulary, verbs, search and examples, both flashcard modes, saved review, speaking/shadowing, story/dialogue playback and Japan Explorer are covered. No global kanji-to-reading replacement.",
    "Kanji detail and JLPT popups offer separate labeled on/kun reading audio; their main audio identifies the chosen study reading. Standalone numerals retain on-yomi; contextual words retain their own readings.",
    "Flashcard APIs and review records preserve a dedicated untruncated reading. Kana/radical deck readings exclude type/position metadata. Exam feedback/review uses available sentence furigana. Grammar patterns and examples keep separate audio controls.",
    "Verified display-copy repair for 名: kun-yomi な; on-yomi メイ/ミョウ retained. Kanjipedia https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kanji/0006666900 agrees with the existing JLPT dataset. Canonical source snapshots remain unchanged.",
    "Roadmap Back returns to the opened chapter/section and restores its scroll position, including browser/BFCache returns, native first-card/completed Back and confirmed exit from unfinished roadmap practice. Fragment/font layout cannot override the restored position; explicit stage jumps remain independent."
  ],
